# race-practice-mc-silence: two races on DIFFERENT courses in one run.
#
# Why PRACTICE and not GP: GP never exposes the track cursor (course_select.c:731-747), and its
# retire card restarts course 1, so a GP replay can only ever race one course (measured:
# docs/research/native/texcacheinterp-progress.md, run R0). PRACTICE's retire overlay carries a
# "Change Course" entry that returns to SELECT COURSE with the track cursor live, so one replay
# can race JACK 1 (MUTE CITY) and then JACK 2 (SILENCE).
#
# What it is for: every per-race buffer that is rewritten in place for the second course --
# `sCourseMinimapTex` above all, a plain u8[0x1000] uploaded as two CI8 blocks and explicitly
# invalidated at minimap.c:201-205 -- is an address the texture cache has already keyed. The
# SHOTs in each race window sample the in-race HUD, where the minimap is drawn.
# SHOT PLACEMENT IS NOT AUTHORED HERE ANY MORE (NEXT.md B15/B43, coverage2-progress.md).
# This file is the INPUT script: ticks, buttons, sticks. The schedule that decides which frames
# the parity gate hashes is DERIVED from a `[debug] cov=1` coverage census of the replay and
# written into the .gdxrec by tools/dev/covsched.py. Regenerating a .gdxrec from this file
# therefore produces a recording with NO SHOTs; re-apply the schedule with
#   tools/dev/covsched.py derive <cov-run>/log-*.txt --rewrite in.gdxrec out.gdxrec
# The hand-placed schedules this file used to carry covered 49-80% of what their replay draws.
build native/texcacheinterp@9f06edc
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=0 rival_detail_auto=0 stereo=1 fh_every=0
at 400
press START 15 0
at 700
press RIGHT 12 0
at 800
press DOWN 12 0
at 1000
press A 15 0
at 1300
press A 15 0
at 1600
press A 15 0
at 1900
press A 15 0
at 2100
wait 1
at 2200
press A 15 0
at 2500
press A 15 0
at 2800
press A 15 0
at 3100
press A 15 0
at 3400
press A 15 0
at 3700
press A 15 0
# --- race 1: MUTE CITY (JACK 1) ---
at 3900
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
wait 200
# --- retire overlay: Retry / Settings / Change Machine / Change Course / Quit ---
at 5600
press DOWN 12 0
at 5750
press DOWN 12 0
at 5900
press DOWN 12 0
at 6000
at 6050
press A 15 0
at 6200
at 6350
press A 15 0
at 6500
press RIGHT 12 0
at 6600
at 6700
press A 15 0
at 7000
press A 15 0
at 7300
press A 15 0
at 7600
press A 15 0
at 7900
press A 15 0
at 8200
press A 15 0
at 8500
press A 15 0
# --- race 2: SILENCE (JACK 2) ---
at 8700
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
hold A 200
wait 200
len 10500
